# Line-ending baseline (EF-17). Text normalizes to LF in the repository and
# checks out per-platform; binary formats are marked so Git never rewrites or
# diffs them as text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Documents — binary. Office formats are ZIP containers: a line-ending rewrite
# corrupts them, and a textual diff is noise either way.
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.doc   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.pptx  binary
*.ppt   binary
*.odt   binary
*.ods   binary
*.odp   binary
*.rtf   binary

# Images
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.bmp   binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.heic  binary

# Scans and audio/video attachments commonly filed with records
*.mp3   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.mov   binary
*.wav   binary

# Archives
*.zip   binary
*.7z    binary
*.gz    binary
*.tar   binary

# Fonts
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

# Git LFS is deliberately NOT configured here. It requires server-side support
# and changes clone behaviour for everyone, so it is an opt-in decision rather
# than a default. Consider it when a binary is large or changes often; see
# records-conventions.md.
